          "name": "Mike Emslie",
          "search_text": "mike emslie severe gbr wide impacts from the 2024 mass coral bleaching event despite recent reports of record-high hard coral cover on the great barrier reef (gbr), the summer of 2024 saw the fifth mass coral bleaching event since 2016, part of the fourth global mass bleaching event. this event exposed some parts of the gbr to unprecedented levels of heat stress, and the broadest spatial footprint of bleaching recorded to date. we document substantial coral mortality directly linked to the severity of thermal stress and bleaching observed at the peak of the event. coral loss ranged from 4% to 72% of pre-bleaching levels among individual reefs, with the northern and central gbr most severely affected. many losses represent the most severe single-event declines in coral cover since monitoring began and highlight the impacts of increasing frequency and severity of climate-driven disturbances. these findings reinforce the urgent need for global emissions reductions to limit warming to 1.5\u20132\u00b0c and preserve coral reef ecosystems.",
