          "search_text": "zahir ridwan kapoposang island and the coral reefs movement a review of community groups driving spider web conservation kapoposang island is one the islands in the spermonde archipelago. its beauty truly attracts the attention of both locals and international visitors, especially its coral reefs and surrounding marine life. there are approximately 120 islands decorating spemonde.\r\n\r\nit is located on the western coast of south sulawesi province in indonesia.  this island with over 400 inhabitants, almost all of its inhabitants are fisherman. this island is relatively not too hot and has lush vegetation. its coastal area is special because it has stretches of exotic coral reefs. \r\n\r\nthe silhouette of the sea is very captivating, all that beauty becomes an opportunity for research and coral reef conservation efforts. \r\n\r\non this island, there is a community movement concerned with coral reef conservation, known as the web spider conservation activist community. it was established in 2015 and has carried out numerous conservation efforts using coral reef duplication methods. by taking a sample from the core, the duplication process then begins with a web-like spider network. \r\n\r\nthrough this effort, we hope to contribute to the preservation of the marine environment in the spermonde archipelago area, and more, specifically on kapoposang island.",
