          "name": "Pooven Muruga",
          "search_text": "pooven muruga fishes and corals: rethinking the narrative surrounding an iconic relationship within tropical, shallow water coral reefs, the relationship between fishes and live corals is arguably the most iconic and highly scrutinized. a strong relationship between fishes and reef-building hard corals is often assumed, a belief supported by studies that document the decline of reef fishes following coral loss. however, the extent of this relationship is often unclear, as evidenced by conflicting reports. here, i present works from my phd that argue for a rethink of this relationship. beginning with a classification of extant fishes into their association with live coral, we highlight that only a small proportion of fishes are closely associated with corals, aligning with published literature. using this classification, we examine the diversification of fishes and corals across evolutionary timescales (~millions of years). we find that fish lineages that rely on coral were decoupled from coral lineage trajectories, challenging co-evolutionary diversification theories.  fast forward to the present, we explore potential confounders that regulate both fish and coral communities globally, highlighting how ecological and evolutionary drivers explain away much of the relationship between these two groups. we then also document changes in fish communities (abundance and species richness) across 1485 sites in 67 locations globally. remarkably, we find decadal stability of fish populations from ecoregions up to major biogeographic realms, with population trajectories largely decoupled from mass coral bleaching events. lastly, we investigate the magnitude of this fish-coral relationship through a meta-analysis of published literature since the 1980s. interestingly, across trophic and taxonomic groupings, we find consistently weak associations with coral cover, even among \u201ccoral-dependent\u201d groups. these findings challenge the longstanding narrative of a critical interdependence between fishes and corals, urging consideration of other factors influencing coral reef systems.",
