        {
          "name": "Mei-Fang Lin",
          "search_text": "mei-fang lin molecular adaptation of reef-building coral leptoria phrygia to localized thermal anomalies coral reef resilience depends on the ability of corals to withstand and adapt to environmental conditions. as reefs face intensifying climate change and local disturbances, understanding the molecular mechanisms underlying resilience has become essential. in southern taiwan, corals experience both global warming and localized thermal stress from a nuclear power plant (nppol), which elevates seawater temperatures and increases daily variability. to investigate adaptive strategies, we sequenced the genome of the common coral leptoria phrygia and integrated transcriptomic analyses across consecutive seasons with population genetic analyses. as expected, corals at the variable nppol site were exposed to greater thermal fluctuations than those at the adjacent stable reef (wlt). despite high connectivity and low genetic differentiation between sites, l. phrygia exhibited distinct transcriptional responses. gene ontology enrichment revealed seasonal shifts in stress responses, apoptosis, cytoskeletal remodeling, and energy metabolism linked to the tricarboxylic acid (tca) cycle, with stress-related pathways enriched in summer and winter. in contrast, autumn and spring featured upregulation of lipid metabolism and biosynthetic pathways, suggesting seasonal reallocation of resources toward energy storage, growth, and reproduction. comparative analysis of field and complementary aquarium tank experimental data identified a core set of differentially expressed genes, including vitellogenins, as potential biomarkers of reproductive status and stress resilience, as well as genes linked to ca2+ homeostasis and tca cycle, suggesting a symbiosis-mediated adaptation strategy. these findings indicate that l. phrygia maintains resilience through transcriptional plasticity rather than genetic differentiation, a strategy that may enhance the coral persistence under ongoing climate change.",
          "talk_titles": [
            {
              "title": "Molecular adaptation of reef-building coral Leptoria phrygia to localized thermal anomalies",
              "primary": true,
              "talk_id": "ac154c51-a758-4fbd-bf36-05e829dc452e"
            }
          ]
        }
