          "name": "Alexandra Butler",
          "search_text": "alexandra butler investigating the effects of predator-prey community structure on carbon sequestration in philippine grazing halos grazing halos\u2013heavily grazed \u2018sandy rings\u2019 around patch reefs\u2013 have been identified as indicators for coral reef ecosystem processes due to their visibility from satellite imagery, prevalence in marine reserves, and formation caused by multi-trophic species interactions. one of the most studied mechanisms behind halo formation is predator induced constrained herbivory, where the fear of predation limits herbivory to areas closest to protection of the reef. trophic cascade theory predicts that this mechanism will cascade to lower trophic levels, ultimately altering macrophyte distribution and associated processes such as carbon cycling. thus, halos may be an indicator not only for intact predator-prey interactions, but also for significant stores of carbon. however, investigating the cascading effects of predators on carbon stocks surrounding halos remains understudied. here, we investigate how predator-prey communities drive halo maintenance and shape organic carbon (oc) stocks in tubbataha reefs natural park (trnp)\u2013the largest no-take sanctuary in the philippines. we hypothesize that (1) predator abundance and diversity will be greater within the halo while apex predators will be more abundant outside of the halo, (2) herbivore abundance, diversity, and bite rate will decrease with increasing distance from the reef, and (3) seagrass percent cover, blade height, and oc stocks will be greater in high predation risk areas (i.e., outside of the halo). this study provides the first assessment of grazing halos, predator-prey interactions, and oc stocks within trnp\u2019s lagoons. addressing these hypotheses will fill critical gaps in understanding how predator-prey interactions can preserve ecosystem processes. further, we aim to inform the use of halo patterns and predator protections as a natural solution to enhance oc stocks.",
