        {
          "name": "Thomas Johnstone",
          "search_text": "thomas johnstone temporal variations in the foraging behaviour of the coral reef mesopredator pseudochromis fuscus mesopredators play a vital role in marine food webs and are an important link between trophic levels. on coral reefs, small carnivorous fish are important mesopredators and exert strong, top down pressure regulating prey communities. however, despite this importance, few studies have directly examined the foraging ecology of small, coral reef meso-predators. to better understand this, we examined the foraging behaviour of pseudochromis fuscus (the dusky dottyback) over three ecologically important temporal periods (the full moon, coral spawning, and the new moon) at lizard island on the great barrier reef, australia. we conducted a total of 56 one hour observations, each focusing on the number of strikes and successful predation attempts directed at coral reef fish recruits and invertebrates. contrary to previous research, we did not observe a successful capture of a coral reef fish recruit, despite p. fuscus displaying a similar strike rate to previously published research. we observed that  strikes directed at invertebrates were common, and consistent across all three temporal periods, and conclude that invertebrates therefore constitute a stable food source. interestingly, there were significantly fewer attempted strikes on coral reef fish recruits during the coral spawning period, likely due to the influx of lipid-rich food. we also observed little difference in foraging behaviour between p. fuscus colour morphs, sizes, or at different times of day. these findings reveal that the foraging behaviour of p. fuscus can be highly variable temporally and may play less of a role in the mortality rates of newly, settled coral reef fish than previously thought. quantifying these interactions is crucial for understanding the ecological interactions of coral reef ecosystems, especially in light of significant environmental change.",
          "talk_titles": [
            {
              "title": "Temporal variations in the foraging behaviour of the coral reef mesopredator Pseudochromis fuscus",
              "primary": true,
              "talk_id": "ff36121e-e72a-45f2-9bed-40ecec669367"
            }
          ]
        }
