          "name": "Mareike Huhn",
          "search_text": "mareike huhn cosmarindo: enhancing coral spawning monitoring and sustainable restoration efforts across indonesia with 16% of the world\u2019s coral reef area, indonesia is tied with australia for the largest coral reef system of any country in the world and is tied with the philippines for the highest diversity in corals. however, public awareness on good practices surrounding reef restoration remains limited. data on coral spawning \u2013 critical for understanding reef resilience and guiding larval-based restoration \u2013 has been limited to very few regions and observations. especially reproduction patterns in mesophotic reefs are largely unknown. to address these gaps, we established the coral spawning monitoring and awareness for restoration network indonesia (cosmarindo), a nationwide, cordap funded initiative designed to build capacity, generate coral spawning data, and promote scientifically grounded restoration practices. after one year, cosmarindo has grown into a network spanning six universities, non-profit organizations, coral reef associated businesses, and independent researchers across indonesia. members actively exchange knowledge on spawning monitoring techniques, species identification, and restoration strategies. a web-based platform \u2018coralog\u2019 for reporting spawning events was launched, resulting in 189 logged observations from 12 organizations within its first month. a camera system for remote monitoring in mesophotic depths was developed. capacity-building efforts included five days of online workshops on coral reproduction, spawning monitoring, reef restoration, and larval propagation with over 100 participants daily, as well as coral identification workshops at six sites from bali to the moluccas, each engaging 15 \u2013 30 participants. cosmarindo demonstrates that collaborative networks, standardized monitoring, and targeted training can rapidly strengthen indonesia\u2019s readiness for and contribution to science-based coral restoration while generating much-needed coral reproduction data across both shallow and mesophotic reef habitats.",
