      "speaker_details": [
        {
          "name": "Fernanda Silva",
          "search_text": "fernanda silva global sensitivity of reef fish species to multiple climate-related pressures the climate crisis has far-reaching consequences for the health and integrity of ecosystems. in marine systems, warming causes shifts in species distributions and interactions, ultimately altering the structure and functioning of marine food webs and ecosystems. the response and sensitivity of reef fish organisms to climate change have commonly been assessed using temperature-based indices. however, the exclusive focus on temperature overlooks effects of other key environmental stressors affecting marine life (e.g, deoxygenation and freshening). here, we introduce a new and integrative framework to quantify reef fish sensitivity to multiple climate-related stressors. using a global dataset of over 3,200 reef species from aquamaps, we estimate single and cumulative environmental safety margins (esms) for temperature, oxygen, and salinity across reef habitats worldwide. we find esms and their underlying stressors to differ between marine ecoregions with generally unsafe conditions in lower latitudes, oceanic islands and estuarine systems. furthermore, we demonstrate regional differences in the relative importance of environmental stressors, where temperature, oxygen limitation and low salinities constrain species and communities differently across marine provinces. reef areas with higher safety margins are characterized by species with large body size, high trophic levels, late maturation and high fecundity. these results show that vulnerability is driven not by a single environmental factor but by a combination of stressors and species-specific adaptations shaped by historical and current oceanographic conditions. the esms approach provide a quantitative, global-scale assessment of climate risk, highlighting priority regions for conservation fulfilling the global target of 30% protection of marine and coastal areas by 2030.",
          "talk_titles": [
            {
              "title": "Global sensitivity of reef fish species to multiple climate-related pressures",
              "primary": true,
              "talk_id": "d78be5f3-b40c-46e4-a1ec-4d02780714cc"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "speaker_count": 1,
