          "name": "Lara Virginia Birkart",
          "search_text": "lara virginia birkart global heatwave causes acropora palmata mass mortality and drastic reduction of reef calcification in 2023, a global marine heat wave caused the fourth and worst mass coral bleaching event, which particularly devastated caribbean reefs. shallow waters were subjected to such extreme heat stress that the caribbean keystone coral, acropora palmata, perished in many areas, with vast implications for reef-building processes. we took aerial images with a commercial drone before, during, and after the marine heatwave to analyze the spatial patterns of a. palmata bleaching and mortality at the reefscape scale of puerto morelos, quintana roo. we then calculated the implied loss in reef calcification potential using a. palmata-specific caco\u2083 production rates. following, we extended our analysis to the greater caribbean using satellite-derived thermal stress data to estimate regional mortality trends throughout the potential shallow-water distributional range of the species. in puerto morelos, the extreme thermal stress (> 14 dhw) caused 100 % a. palmata mortality (1,193 m\u00b2) which translates to an overall loss of 21,400 kg of caco\u2083 per year. nearly 70 % of reef crests in the greater caribbean experienced thermal stress levels equal to or greater than puerto morelos which indicates a catastrophic mass mortality event for the species and a drastic reduction in reef-building processes. science-based and inclusive monitoring, restoration, and conservation, in combination with actions against climate change, are required to ensure the future of a. palmata in our lives.",
