          "name": "Evan Heit",
          "search_text": "evan heit comprehensive analysis of the coral metabolome directed at understanding climate resilience coral reefs face severe threats from climate change, underlying the need to understand the mechanisms behind coral stress responses and resilience. metabolomic approaches are increasingly being used to fill this knowledge gap. however, key challenges around sample preparation and throughput as well as metabolite coverage and annotation remain. we developed a high-throughput, comprehensive liquid chromatography-mass spectrometry pipeline for analyzing coral samples (host and algal symbiont), and generated baseline metabolomics data on the corals galaxea fascicularis and pocillopora acuta. metabolic changes in the host and symbiont fraction were also monitored over three weeks (five timepoints) at ambient temperature (27 \u00b0c) or under a gradual increase in temperature from 27 \u00b0c to 32 \u00b0c. the elevated temperature treatment resulted in heat stress as confirmed by a decline in photosynthetic health, cell density, and protein concentrations. unique metabolomic profiles were observed in both the heat-stressed coral host and symbiont, with changes in the host fraction being more pronounced. heat stress led to changes in intermediates in host glycolysis and tca cycle (including citrate, pep, cis-aconitate and succinate). alterations in metabolic fluxes were also detected by labelling coral polyps with heavy water, providing an orthogonal approach for assessing changes in coral central carbon metabolism in response to heat stress.",
