          "name": "Bill Leggat",
          "search_text": "bill leggat recovery from bleaching for sub-tropical corals in the era of climate change coral reefs around the world are predicted to experience increased frequency of bleaching events. given this it is key if we are to understand future coral reef ecosystem structure we must understand how corals recovery from bleaching events. as with other reefs around the world the sub-tropical reefs of norfolk island and lord howe have experience repeated coral bleaching events over the last 6 years. this study examines how the coral reef populations recovery from bleaching events. the results highlight that recovery time in sub-tropical reefs is significantly slower than that seen in topical reefs with substantially different recovery rates between different species. these slower recovery rates mean that sub-tropical reefs are uniquely vulnerable to repeated coral bleaching events as recovery may not have occurred before subsequent bleaching events,",
