          "search_text": "zoe meziere genomic repeatability and predictability of local (mal)adaptation in a reef-building coral although local adaptation is widely recognised as a central process shaping genetic diversity, its genetic basis and ecological implications remain poorly understood. here, we integrate whole-genome sequencing, genotype\u2013environment associations, and predictive modelling to investigate climate adaptation in stylophora pistillata corals sampled across the great barrier reef. we characterise the genomic architecture of thermal adaptation across populations and show that populations rely on different combinations of putatively adaptive genomic regions. we find that genotype\u2013environment relationships inferred from geographically broad sampling can reliably predict local adaptation patterns across space and forward in time. importantly, we provide the most spatially explicit quantification of genomic vulnerability under future warming scenarios for a coral species. together, our results offer novel insights into the genomic basis of coral adaptation and highlight the value of integrating evolutionary principles in coral reef ecological forecasting.",
