          "name": "Jokim Kitolelei",
          "search_text": "jokim kitolelei coral boundaries as ecological frontiers: fijian communities conserving reefs and keystone species coral reefs function as a vital ecological markers and natural boundaries for marine resource users. this research explores how fijian communities identify their fishing boundaries, delineate, utilize, and manage their reef systems through traditional ecological knowledge rather than modern technological tools. rooted in generational wisdom, leadership guidance, and intimate familiarity with local environments, these practices enable communities to sustain reef health and protect keystone species. the study highlights adaptive strategies that reinforce resilience, cultural identity, and ecological stewardship, particularly in reefs located near villages where marine activities and cultural practices intersect. findings underscore the critical role of indigenous knowledge in shaping contemporary reef management frameworks, offering pathways to strengthen conservation and community-based governance in the face of ongoing environmental challenges.",
