          "name": "Marilyn Brandt",
          "search_text": "marilyn brandt cracking the code of coral disease: an integrated experimental and field-based approach to understanding coral disease marine diseases have decimated marine coastal ecosystems, including coral reefs. the pathogens driving these diseases have frequently been challenging to confirm, in part because they affect multiple host species and spread by ocean currents. our interdisciplinary team\u2013comprising ecologists, modelers, microbiologists, and immunologists\u2013has developed an approach to studying coral disease that captures both within-coral and between-coral dynamics. we have applied this framework to wp, sctld, and an unidentified disease outbreak in the gulf of mexico. to understand wp and sctld, we began by conducting transmission experiments that revealed key information on species susceptibility, dysbiosis, and the timing of immune responses. more recently, we have expanded our approach to field sampling missions, where tracking the fate of sampled corals is offering deeper insight into how coral- and community-level traits shape disease dynamics and shed light on their etiologies.",
